 "notes": [
  "Not broken out: GPIO11 and GPIO12-17 (GPIO12-17: SPI flash); all other GPIOs are on J1/J3.",
  "GPIO2, GPIO8 and GPIO9 are strapping pins; GPIO8 also drives the on-board RGB LED.",
  "TX/RX (GPIO21/GPIO20) are U0TXD/U0RXD.",
  "GPIO18/19 are USB_D-/USB_D+ (USB-Serial/JTAG by default) on J3-13/J3-14.",
  "GPIO5 is the only ADC2 pin (ADC2_CH0); ESP-IDF no longer supports ADC2 oneshot mode on the ESP32-C3, so use ADC1 on GPIO0-4.",
  "GPIO4-7 carry MTMS, MTDI, MTCK and MTDO (pad JTAG).",
  "Pins are checked for ESP32-C3-MINI-1 (ESP32-C3-DevKitM-1-N4X: 4 MB flash in the chip package, no PSRAM); the guide also names ESP32-C3-MINI-1U with an external antenna connector.",
  "The user guide text does not name the USB-to-UART bridge chip; its pin layout figure shows a chip marked CP2102 (read from the figure, unverified)."
 ],
